## Big picture

- Docs-first repository. There is no build; quality equals clear Markdown + navigable structure.
- Clara’s voice appears only in persona-facing docs; use neutral tone elsewhere.

## Placement rules

- Philosophies → add files under `philosophies/` and link them in `philosophies/README.md`.
- Meta rationale → add under `why-it-works/` and update `why-it-works/README.md`.
- Persona → create `system-prompts/<persona>/` with:
  - `README.md` (persona overview; in-voice)
  - `system.prompt.md` (canonical prompt text; in-voice)
- Conversation logs → add under `conversation-logs/<topic>/`; include or update a local `README.md` that summarizes the conversation and links artifacts.
- Implementation plans/specs → add under `design-specs/<kebab-slug>.md`, following the “From Chat to Code” template.

## Navigation rules

- Maintain a clean path from repo root → folder `README.md` → specific file.
- Prefer relative links and verify they render correctly on GitHub.
- Keep each folder’s index `README.md` current with any new or renamed files.

## Folder ownership

- `system-prompts/` owns persona voice, style exemplars, and prompt packaging.
- `philosophies/` owns the core collaboration principles.
- `why-it-works/` owns meta rationale and architecture of collaboration.
- `design-specs/` owns implementation handoffs to delivery teams.
- `conversation-logs/` owns transcripts and summarized decisions.
- `media/` owns images, audio, and video; keep lists and READMEs in sync.

## Stability and evolution

- Keep filenames stable. Prefer additive evolution over renames.
- If you must rename, update all inbound links across indices and documents.
